### 🐛 Current behavior

Catch all routes with "react-instantsearch-hooks-router-nextjs" do not work. The browser button does not work at all.

@aymeric-giraudet I tried solving it with your beforePopState solution. But this does not even get triggered. 

### 🔍 Steps to reproduce

Create a [...all].js in pages.js

Then make the instant search pages use the same catch all route as the hit.

The fix is in https://github.com/algolia/instantsearch/blob/master/packages/instantsearch.js/src/lib/routers/history.ts =>

Problem is

`  public dispose(): void {
    if (this._dispose) {
      this._dispose();
    }

    this.isDisposed = true;

    safelyRunOnBrowser(({ window }) => {
      if (this._onPopState) {
        window.removeEventListener('popstate', this._onPopState);
      }
    });

    if (this.writeTimer) {
      clearTimeout(this.writeTimer);
    }

    this.write({} as TRouteState);
  }`

This last rule should not be there for next to work.

`
    this.write({} as TRouteState);
`
When I comment this line everything works as expected.

### Live reproduction

https://codesandbox.io/s/github/algolia/instantsearch.js/tree/templates/react-instantsearch

### 💭 Expected behavior

Catch all routes with getStaticProps should work.

### Package version

next 13.3.0, react-instantsearch-hooks-router-nextjs 6.42.1, react-instantsearch-hooks-server 6.42.1, react-instantsearch-hooks-web 6.42.1

